          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 29. Current seizure frequency is approximately six seizures per week.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Lamotrigine\n- Perampanel\n\nSeizure Burden:\nGeneralized tonic-clonic seizures occur approximately six times weekly despite the current antiseizure medication regimen.\n\nAssessment:\n- Drug-resistant generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures\n- Structural etiology\n- MRI finding consistent with focal cortical dysplasia, Palmini type IIb\n\nPlan:\nContinue the current antiseizure medications, lamotrigine and perampanel, with ongoing monitoring of seizure burden.",
